ent-RUMCCopperWireItem = fine copper wire
    .desc = A thin copper wire. Circuits, cables and windings are made of it.
ent-RUMCGoldWireItem = fine gold wire
    .desc = A thin gold wire that does not corrode.
ent-RUMCSilverWireItem = fine silver wire
    .desc = A thin silver wire, the best conductor there is.
ent-RUMCIronRodItem = steel rod
    .desc = A turned steel rod.
ent-RUMCMagneticRodItem = magnetic rod
    .desc = A steel rod that has been magnetized. The heart of every electric motor.
ent-RUMCIronBoltItem = steel bolt
    .desc = A short steel bolt cut from a rod.
ent-RUMCIronScrewItem = steel screw
    .desc = A steel screw turned from a bolt.
ent-RUMCThermoAlloyItem = heat-resistant alloy ingot
    .desc = An alloy of chromium and steel that glows red without melting. The coils of the furnaces are wound of it.
ent-RUMCConductorAlloyItem = conductor alloy ingot
    .desc = An alloy of copper and silver that carries current well. It goes into vacuum tubes.
ent-RUMCRawRubberItem = raw rubber
    .desc = Sticky raw rubber extracted from resin. It is vulcanized with cinnabar into rubber sheets.
ent-RUMCRubberSheetItem = rubber sheet
    .desc = A sheet of vulcanized rubber. It insulates.
ent-RUMCInsulatedCableItem = insulated cable
    .desc = A copper wire in a rubber sheath.
ent-RUMCGlassTubeItem = glass tube
    .desc = A thin glass tube for a vacuum lamp.
ent-RUMCVacuumTubeItem = vacuum tube
    .desc = A vacuum lamp: the first circuit element of the electric age.
ent-RUMCResistorItem = resistor
    .desc = A small carbon resistor.
ent-RUMCSiliconIngotItem = silicon ingot
    .desc = Pure silicon smelted from quartz or sand.
ent-RUMCSiliconWaferItem = silicon wafer
    .desc = A thin wafer of silicon for diodes.
ent-RUMCDiodeItem = diode
    .desc = A silicon diode: current goes through it one way only.
ent-RUMCResinBoardItem = resin circuit board
    .desc = A wooden board bonded with rubber and wired with copper: the base of the first circuits.
ent-RUMCPhenolicBoardItem = phenolic circuit board
    .desc = A better board of glue-soaked wood with silver traces: the base of the good circuits.
ent-RUMCBasicCircuitItem = basic electronic circuit
    .desc = The first circuit of the electric age (LV). Every machine of the first tier needs it.
ent-RUMCGoodCircuitItem = good electronic circuit
    .desc = A circuit of the second tier (MV), made of diodes and basic circuits on a phenolic board.
ent-RUMCMotorItem = electric motor
    .desc = A small electric motor of low voltage. Machines are built around it.
ent-RUMCPistonItem = electric piston
    .desc = A piston driven by a motor.
ent-RUMCPumpItem = electric pump
    .desc = A small pump driven by a motor.
ent-RUMCConveyorItem = conveyor module
    .desc = A motorized belt that moves items through a machine.
ent-RUMCHeatingCoilItem = heating coil
    .desc = A coil of wire that glows hot when current runs through it.
ent-RUMCGemDiamondItem = diamond
    .desc = A cut diamond: clear and hard.
ent-RUMCGemEmeraldItem = emerald
    .desc = A cut emerald.
ent-RUMCGemRubyItem = ruby
    .desc = A cut ruby.
ent-RUMCGemAlexandriteItem = alexandrite
    .desc = A cut alexandrite. It plays blue in the lamp and red in the daylight.
ent-RUMCLensDiamondItem = diamond lens
    .desc = A lens ground of a diamond. It engraves the finest patterns.
ent-RUMCLensEmeraldItem = emerald lens
    .desc = A lens ground of an emerald.
ent-RUMCLensRubyItem = ruby lens
    .desc = A lens ground of a ruby: the red light of a laser comes out of it.
ent-RUMCLensAlexandriteItem = alexandrite lens
    .desc = A lens ground of an alexandrite.
ent-RUMCGalvanizedSheetItem = galvanized steel sheet
    .desc = A steel sheet with a coat of zinc that keeps the rust off. Tin cans are made of it.
ent-RUMCChromedSheetItem = chrome-plated steel sheet
    .desc = A steel sheet with a bright coat of chrome. It does not rust and does not stain.
ent-RUMCTinCanItem = tin can
    .desc = An empty can of galvanized steel, ready to be filled and sealed.
ent-RUMCWaferICItem = IC wafer
    .desc = A silicon wafer engraved with a ruby lens: the pattern of an integrated circuit. It is cut into chips.
ent-RUMCWaferULPICItem = ULPIC wafer
    .desc = A silicon wafer engraved with an alexandrite lens: an ultra-low power chip. It is cut into chips.
ent-RUMCWaferRAMItem = RAM wafer
    .desc = A silicon wafer engraved with an emerald lens: memory. It is cut into chips.
ent-RUMCWaferCPUItem = CPU wafer
    .desc = A silicon wafer engraved with a diamond lens: a processor. It is cut into chips.
ent-RUMCChipICItem = IC chip
    .desc = A chip of an integrated circuit.
ent-RUMCChipULPICItem = ULPIC chip
    .desc = An ultra-low power chip.
ent-RUMCChipRAMItem = RAM chip
    .desc = A chip of memory.
ent-RUMCChipCPUItem = CPU chip
    .desc = The chip of a processor.
ent-RUMCTransistorItem = transistor
    .desc = A small transistor that goes onto a circuit board.
ent-RUMCCapacitorItem = capacitor
    .desc = A small capacitor for circuit boards.
ent-RUMCInductorItem = inductor
    .desc = A small coil on a magnetic core. It goes onto circuit boards and into motors.
ent-RUMCIntegratedCircuitItem = integrated circuit
    .desc = A circuit of the low tier that is made in batches: easier than the basic one.
ent-RUMCGoodIntegratedCircuitItem = good integrated circuit
    .desc = A circuit of the second tier, two of them to a craft.
ent-RUMCMicroprocessorItem = microprocessor
    .desc = The best circuit of the second tier (MV): a processor with its transistors and capacitors on a board.
ent-RUMCMachineHullMVItem = MV casing parts
    .desc = Aluminum plates and frames that the casing of a machine of the second tier is made of.
ent-RUMCMotorMVItem = MV electric motor
    .desc = A motor of the second tier: more power out of the same size.
ent-RUMCPlasticPelletsItem = plastic pellets
    .desc = Granules of plastic, the stuff that is pressed into sheets.
ent-RUMCSulfurPowderItem = sulfur powder
    .desc = Yellow sulfur powder. Rubber is vulcanized with it, and acid is made of it.
ent-RUMCIronGearItem = steel gear
    .desc = A cast steel gear.
ent-RUMCIronRingItem = steel ring
    .desc = A cast steel ring.
ent-RUMCMoldRodItem = rod mold
    .desc = A steel mold for the extruder: it presses rods.
ent-RUMCMoldBoltItem = bolt mold
    .desc = A steel mold for the extruder: it presses bolts.
ent-RUMCMoldScrewItem = screw mold
    .desc = A steel mold for the extruder: it presses screws.
ent-RUMCMoldGearItem = gear mold
    .desc = A steel mold for the extruder: it presses gears.
ent-RUMCMoldRingItem = ring mold
    .desc = A steel mold for the extruder: it presses rings.
ent-RUMCPlasticBoardItem = plastic circuit board
    .desc = A board of plastic with a thin film of copper: cheaper than the phenolic one, and every board makes more circuits.
ent-RUMCMachineHullItem = machine casing parts
    .desc = Plates and frames of sheet steel that the casing of a machine of the first tier is made of.
ent-RUMCWiremill = wiremill
    .desc = Draws ingots into fine wire, twice as much as hands could.
ent-RUMCBender = bending machine
    .desc = Presses ingots into sheets. On circuit 2 it presses steel into floor tiles, on circuit 3 into armour plates.
ent-RUMCLathe = lathe
    .desc = Turns a sheet of steel into rods (circuit 1), straight into bolts (circuit 2), into metal rods for building (circuit 3) or forged parts (circuit 4), and bolts into screws.
ent-RUMCCutter = cutting machine
    .desc = Cuts rods into bolts and nails, glass into tubes and silicon into wafers.
ent-RUMCPolarizer = polarizer
    .desc = Magnetizes steel rods.
ent-RUMCExtractor = extractor
    .desc = Presses resin out of wood and turns resin into raw rubber.
ent-RUMCMixer = mixer
    .desc = Mixes metals into alloys and solder, raw rubber with cinnabar into rubber sheets, and flares out of saltpeter, sulfur and paper.
ent-RUMCChemicalReactor = chemical reactor
    .desc = Boils glue out of resin, vulcanizes rubber better than the mixer does, and cooks gunpowder.
ent-RUMCElectricAssembler = assembler
    .desc = Assembles motors, boards, circuits and every other part of the electric age out of smaller ones, and radios, multitools, flashlights, defibrillators and reinforced glass for the colony.
ent-RUMCElectricBlastFurnace = electric blast furnace
    .desc = A furnace of heating coils: it smelts silicon out of quartz or sand and coke.
ent-RUMCOreWasher = ore washer
    .desc = Washes ore in water: the stone is carried off and more of the ore comes out as powder than the grinder gets.
ent-RUMCThermalCentrifuge = thermal centrifuge
    .desc = Spins hot metal powder apart and sorts out the other metal that was in the ore. It eats a lot of power.
ent-RUMCMagneticSeparator = electromagnetic separator
    .desc = Picks the metal that is left in the stone dust out of it.
ent-RUMCSifter = sifter
    .desc = Sorts a crystal into the gem in it without crushing it, and a little powder and stone dust come with it.
ent-RUMCAutoclave = autoclave
    .desc = Grows a gem back out of its powder in water, slowly. It is what to do with the powder of a crystal that was crushed.
ent-RUMCPyrolysisOven = pyrolysis oven
    .desc = Cooks wood, branches and coal without air into coke, and the tar that comes off it is resin.
ent-RUMCGalvanicBath = galvanic bath
    .desc = Coats a steel sheet with zinc or chrome out of its powder in water, with current.
ent-RUMCRecycler = recycler
    .desc = Takes parts and finished things apart and gives back half of the material they were made of. It takes any item.
ent-RUMCFertilizerMixer = fertilizer mixer
    .desc = Dissolves saltpeter and phosphorus in water into a fertilizer that plants take up. Pipe it to an automatic tray.
ent-RUMCCannery = cannery
    .desc = Rolls cans out of galvanized steel and fills them with nutrient paste or protein, then seals them.
ent-RUMCJewelersBench = jeweler's machine
    .desc = Casts gold and silver into rings and sets gems in them.
ent-RUMCLaserEngraver = laser engraver
    .desc = Burns the pattern of a chip into a silicon wafer. The lens in the slot decides which: ruby, alexandrite, emerald or diamond. The lens is not used up.
ent-RUMCElectrolyzer = electrolyzer
    .desc = Splits water into hydrogen and oxygen with current, and cinnabar into sulfur and mercury.
ent-RUMCArcFurnace = arc furnace
    .desc = Smelts glass out of sand and quartz with an arc and a breath of oxygen, and alloys brass, steel of iron sheets and coke, plasteel of steel and coke, and the alloys of the steel family and the heat-resistant one.
ent-RUMCChemicalBath = chemical bath
    .desc = Soaks wood into paper (or, on circuit 1, into cardboard), and etches circuit boards with acid.
ent-RUMCCentrifuge = centrifuge
    .desc = Spins mixtures apart: slag into powder, resin into rubber and glue, cinnabar into sulfur.
ent-RUMCCompressor = compressor
    .desc = Presses powder back into stone, and branches into planks.
ent-RUMCFluidSolidifier = fluid solidifier
    .desc = Lets a molten metal or glass set into ingots and sheets, without a mold.
ent-RUMCExtruder = extruder
    .desc = Presses a sheet of steel through the mold in its slot: rods, bolts, screws, gears or rings. The mold is not used up.
ent-RUMCPharmaMachine = pharmaceutical machine
    .desc = Makes the field-medicine ingredients out of the chemistry (antiseptic, coagulant, burn gel, tissue sealant, trauma foam), plain gauze and dressings out of cloth, and mixes them into the prepared ones.
ent-RUMCConcreteMixer = concrete mixer
    .desc = Mixes stone dust and sand with water into packs of concrete, and casts reinforced ones around metal rods. Build walls of the packs.
ent-RUMCSewingMachine = sewing machine
    .desc = Makes cloth out of cotton, and sews bags, belts, pouches, clothes and sandbags out of cloth, for less cloth than the tailor's table takes.
ent-RUMCTannery = tannery
    .desc = Tans hides in water with chrome powder into leather, and cuts leather into boots and gloves.
ent-RUMCFabricator = complex assembly bench
    .desc = A bench with eighteen slots for materials and one for the finished thing: it assembles the complex hand things out of many parts at once, the electric tools above all.
ent-RUMCCircuitAssembler = circuit assembler
    .desc = The machine that makes circuits properly: cheaper basic circuits and the good ones.
ent-RUMCSteamExtractor = steam extractor
    .desc = An extractor driven by steam. It presses resin out of wood and turns resin into raw rubber, which is how rubber is had before the grid. Join a gas pipe with steam to it.

reagent-name-au14-hydrochloric-acid = hydrochloric acid
reagent-desc-au14-hydrochloric-acid = A strong acid that etches copper off a board.
reagent-name-au14-crude-oil = crude oil
reagent-desc-au14-crude-oil = Black, thick and heavy. It is pumped out of the ground and sent through the distillation tower.
reagent-name-au14-naphtha = naphtha
reagent-desc-au14-naphtha = A light fraction of oil. It is cracked into ethylene.
reagent-name-au14-light-fuel = light fuel
reagent-desc-au14-light-fuel = A light fuel oil. Mixed with the heavy one it makes diesel.
reagent-name-au14-heavy-fuel = heavy fuel
reagent-desc-au14-heavy-fuel = A thick, dark fuel oil.
reagent-name-au14-diesel = diesel
reagent-desc-au14-diesel = The fuel of the diesel generator.
reagent-name-au14-refinery-gas = refinery gas
reagent-desc-au14-refinery-gas = A light gas that comes off the oil.
reagent-name-au14-ethylene = ethylene
reagent-desc-au14-ethylene = A gas that makes plastic.
reagent-name-au14-fertilizer = plant fertilizer
reagent-desc-au14-fertilizer = A solution of saltpeter and phosphorus that feeds plants.
reagent-name-au14-glue = glue
reagent-desc-au14-glue = A sticky glue boiled out of resin.
reagent-name-au14-solder-melt = molten solder
reagent-desc-au14-solder-melt = Molten solder of lead and zinc. It joins the parts of the circuits.

